# 低频词汇 List02
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2023恋练有词
# 描述: 低频词汇List02核心词汇

{{apparatus}}{/ˌæpəˈreɪtəs/}{器械；机构}{The laboratory is equipped with modern scientific apparatus.}}
{{appliance}}{/əˈplaɪəns/}{器具；家用电器}{The kitchen is fitted with energy-efficient appliances.}}
{{applicable}}{/əˈplɪkəbl/}{适用的；可应用的}{This rule is applicable to all employees.}}
{{appreciation}}{/əˌpriːʃiˈeɪʃn/}{欣赏；感激；增值}{She showed her appreciation with a handwritten note.}}
{{arbitrary}}{/ˈɑːbɪtrəri/}{任意的；武断的}{The decision seemed arbitrary and unfair.}}
{{architect}}{/ˈɑːkɪtekt/}{建筑师；设计师}{The architect designed a sustainable office building.}}
{{arithmetic}}{/əˈrɪθmətɪk/}{算术；计算}{Basic arithmetic skills are essential for daily life.}}
{{arrest}}{/əˈrest/}{逮捕；阻止}{The police arrested the suspect at the airport.}}
{{artificial}}{/ˌɑːtɪˈfɪʃl/}{人工的；人造的}{Artificial intelligence is transforming many industries.}}
{{aspire}}{/əˈspaɪər/}{渴望；追求}{She aspires to become a leading expert in her field.}}
{{assault}}{/əˈsɔːlt/}{攻击；袭击}{The assault on the journalist was widely condemned.}}
{{assemble}}{/əˈsembl/}{组装；集合}{Volunteers assembled care packages for the homeless.}}
{{asset}}{/ˈæset/}{资产；有用的东西}{Her experience is a valuable asset to the team.}}
{{assimilate}}{/əˈsɪmɪleɪt/}{同化；吸收}{Immigrants often struggle to assimilate into a new culture.}}
{{assistance}}{/əˈsɪstəns/}{帮助；援助}{The government provides financial assistance to low-income families.}}
{{astonish}}{/əˈstɒnɪʃ/}{使惊讶}{The results astonished the research team.}}
{{astronomy}}{/əˈstrɒnəmi/}{天文学}{Astronomy has fascinated humans for thousands of years.}}
{{athlete}}{/ˈæθliːt/}{运动员}{The athlete broke the world record in the 100-meter dash.}}
{{atlas}}{/ˈætləs/}{地图集}{She opened the atlas to find the location.}}
{{atrocity}}{/əˈtrɒsəti/}{暴行；残忍}{The atrocities committed during the war were documented.}}
{{attendance}}{/əˈtendəns/}{出席；到场}{Attendance at the conference exceeded expectations.}}
{{attribute}}{/ˈætrɪbjuːt/}{属性；特质}{Patience is an important attribute for a teacher.}}
{{auction}}{/ˈɔːkʃn/}{拍卖}{The painting was sold at auction for two million dollars.}}
{{audience}}{/ˈɔːdiəns/}{观众；听众}{The audience gave the performers a standing ovation.}}
{{authentic}}{/ɔːˈθentɪk/}{真实的；可信的}{The museum displays only authentic historical artifacts.}}
{{authorize}}{/ˈɔːθəraɪz/}{授权；批准}{Only the manager can authorize such a large purchase.}}
{{autonomy}}{/ɔːˈtɒnəmi/}{自治；自主权}{The university values academic autonomy.}}
{{aviation}}{/ˌeɪviˈeɪʃn/}{航空；飞行}{The aviation industry was hit hard by the pandemic.}}
{{awkward}}{/ˈɔːkwəd/}{尴尬的；笨拙的}{There was an awkward silence after his remark.}}
{{bachelor}}{/ˈbætʃələr/}{学士；单身汉}{He earned a bachelor's degree in computer science.}}
